            <ArticleTitle>An 8-year-old girl with unilateral facial and ear pain and isolated frontal headaches.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>182-8; discussion 189</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An 8 1/2-year-old with chronic but fluctuating unilateral facial pain, earache, frontal headache and facial swelling is presented. Her journey through the health care system provides an instructional lesson for all who deal with patients with unusual or difficult to recognize conditions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
